From 0ff149c47a28882049b28334c97d70cdad2ca041 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:59:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rpi-firmwared: governor, the ARM clock follows the load

Every 100 ms the governor reads the per-CPU times from sys:stat. Above
50 % load on the busiest CPU it sets the maximum clock, after 2 s below
30 % the minimum. /scheme/rpi-firmware/governor shows mode, target,
load and clock changes; writing ondemand, performance or powersave sets
the mode. Writing arm_clock stops the governor (mode fixed).

Refs redox-rpi/redox-rpi#23

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
